es, Open"] "\n" [:option {:value "51716"} "Free Rifle, Three Positions, 300 metres, Open"] "\n" [:option {:value "51712"} "Small-Bore Rifle, Three Positions, 50 metres, Open"] "\n" [:option {:value "51711"} "Small-Bore Rifle, Prone, 50 metres, Open"] "\n" [:option {:value "51720"} "Trap, Open"]] [:script {} "$('#same_games_select').change(function(){location.href='/results/' + $('#same_games_select').val();})"]] " | " [:form {:class "form-inline form-inline-header"} [:select {:name "id", :id "other_games_select", :class "form-control"} [:option {:value ""} "In other Games"] "\n" [:option {:value "51735"} "1972"] "\n" [:option {:value "51745"} "1976"] "\n" [:option {:value "51756"} "1980"] "\n" [:option {:value "51769"} "1984"] "\n" [:option {:value "51807"} "1988"] "\n" [:option {:value "51855"} "1992"]] [:script {} "$('#other_games_select').change(function(){location.href='/results/' + $('#other_games_select').val();})"]] " | " [:a {:href "/event_names/515"} "Event type"]] [:h1 {:class "event_title"} "Skeet, Open" [:small {}]] [:table {:class "biodata"} [:tbody {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Date"] [:td {} "21 – 22 October 1968 — 8:30"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Status"] [:td {} "Olympic"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Location"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/venues/496"} "Polígono de Tiro Vicente Suárez, Campo Militar No. 1, Ciudad de México"]]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Participants"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/events/51721"} "52 from 30 countries"]]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Format"] [:td {:colspan "2"} "200 targets."]]]] [:div {:class "description"} [:p {} "This was the Olympic début for skeet shooting. It is somewhat similar to trap shooting as the shooters used a shotgun to fire at clay discs. But in skeet, the rifle is held at the hip, or mid-torso, until the target is fired and the birds are thrown from two towers above the ground, while trap discs are launched from ground level. In skeet, there is also a variable delay for the discs to be launched after they are called."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Most of the shooters used the Browning over-and-under shotgun, with the German Rottweil the most popular ammunition. At the 1967 World Championships, Germany’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/42605"} "Konrad Wirnhier"] " was the champion, with Soviets " [:a {:href "/athletes/44558"} "Yury Tsuranov"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/44540"} "Yevgeny Petrov"] " placing second and third, respectively. On the first day, Chile’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/41568"} "Jorge Jottar"] " led with 99, followed by Petrov, Wirnhier and Italy’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/42976"} "Romano Garagnani"] " with 98. Jottar fell back on the second day, while Petrov, Wirnhier and Garagnani were clean to tie for first at 198, Tsuranov finishing fourth with 196. In the shoot-off Petrov won the gold medal with a clean 25 string, while Garagnani took the silver in a second round of shoot-offs."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "Points"] [:th {} "Round 1 Points"] [:th {} "Round 2 Points"] [:th {} "Round 3 Points"] [:th {} "Round 4 Points"] [:th {} "Round 5 Points"] [:th {} "Round 6 Points"] [:th {} "Round 7 Points"] [:th {} "Round 8 Points"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/44540"} "Yevgeny Petrov"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/URS"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/URS.png"}] "URS"]] [:td {} "198"] [:td {} "24"] [:td {} "25"] [:td {} "25"] [:td {} "24"] [:td {} "25"] [:td {} "25"] [:td {} "25"] [:td {} "25"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "label label-default"} [:abbrev {:title "World Record (equalled)"} "=WR"]]] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/42976"} "Romano Garagnani"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/ITA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-cen